// The MG90S is a 180-degree servo (no continuous spin), and the inlet (top) and
// outlet (bottom) are 180 degrees apart. A SMALL sweep + return has zero net
// rotation, so a pocket filled at the inlet could never reach the outlet -- it
// would dispense once then dead-head. So the firmware uses a FULL 180-degree
// oscillation with a dwell at each end: forward carries the inlet pocket down
// to the outlet and drops it; the pocket now at the inlet fills during the
// dwell; the return carries THAT one down and drops it. One cycle ~= 2 pockets,
// consistent cycle-to-cycle -> calibrate GRAMS_PER_CYCLE (weigh one cycle).
